experience.description:
Over the past 10 years, my financial transaction experience has included: initial public offerings for domestic and foreign private issuers (FPIs), SEC 144A private debt placements, mergers, acquisitions, joint ventures, application of fresh-start accounting and bankruptcy reporting (reorganizations and restructurings), restatements, leveraged buy-outs, asset impairments, purchase price allocations, and business disposals (spin-offs, split-offs, split-ups, and equity carve-outs). 

Representative areas of advice and analyses provided to senior executives:
► assessing the accounting and financial statement impact of proposed transaction structures under U.S. GAAP and IFRS;
► providing SEC filing support assistance on accounting and financial reporting matters;
► assisting with the research for and drafting of position papers (white papers) to support critical financial transaction matters (and serve as credible and persuasive audit evidence); 
► critically evaluating the people, process, and technology needs of key functional business areas, providing gap analysis and observations for areas such accounting and financial reporting; financial planning and analysis (FP&A); compliance, corporate governance, and risk management; equity story and investor relations; treasury; human resources; and information technology;
► providing recommendations to stabilize or remediate deficiencies found in these areas;
► preparing benchmarking analyses against peers companies (for metrics such as key performance indicators); and
► providing educational guidance on technical accounting matters.

